From 345e007a2efec6918d7745047951dfce880840cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nova <361320585+q2-nova@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:38:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] ASoC: add X2000 BAIC1 playback and Shanling Q2 sound
 card

Implement DMA0 through DSP source 8/timeslot 9 to BAIC1, following the
stock single cyclic descriptor and polled DMA pointer protocol. Expose
stereo S16_LE/S24_LE/S32_LE at 44.1/48/96 kHz with bounded buffer/period
sizes. Synchronize timer cancellation before buffer release.

Connect four CS43131 endpoints with the stock left/right copy and
inverted-B routing. Add standard mixer controls, shared PB14 reset,
PB1 coarse DAC supply enable and output mute/mode control. PB2 stays low;
its stock high-volume boost policy is not implemented. Enable runtime
PM, with system suspend disabled, and add validated audio DT schemas.

Generated ALSA ioctl tests pass byte-exact PCM, pause/resume, polling
drain, deliberate underrun/recovery, close/reset and reopen/cache restore.
Display and SMP/storage/buttons/power/backlight regressions pass. These
are emulator results. FIFO/drain accuracy, descriptor interrupt encoding,
individual physical rails, analog routing, output timing and DMA cache
coherency remain hardware/model qualification items.
